  "derivation": "E_data[product_i P(mu_i|phi)] = (sum_mu q_mu P(mu|phi))^p. Normalizing each p-record posterior before averaging is a different operation. Product of individually normalized one-measurement posteriors gives another kernel with Z_mu. Expected log likelihood is a further, distinct Asimov statistic. None is silently equated with mean68% width."
